course: dictionary
lesson: 11578
title: Annul: cancelling as if it never happened
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are about rules, and you may meet them in the news or in history. Annul is one of these. When you meet a new word, read the words around it: they are its context, and they leave clues. «The judge decided to annul the election after the rules were broken.» The judge stopped the election, and the rules were broken, so annul must mean to cancel it.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. Try: «The judge decided to cancel the election.» It still makes sense, so cancel is a good meaning for annul. Annul is stronger than just stopping something. It means the thing is treated as if it never counted at all.
explain: Annul is a verb, so it changes: annuls, annulled, annulling. The noun is annulment. «The annulment of the contract was announced today.» Here the annulment is the act of cancelling the contract.
fact: Annul means to officially say that something never counted and is cancelled.
fact: You can annul things such as a marriage, a contract, or an election.
fact: In the Catholic Church, an annulment declares that a marriage was never valid.
fact: In history, Henry VIII wanted the Pope to annul his marriage to Catherine of Aragon. When the Pope said no, England broke away from the Catholic Church.
fact: The noun form is «annulment», and the verb forms are «annuls», «annulled» and «annulling».
exercise: «The judge decided to annul the election after the rules were broken.» What does annul mean here? | To run the election again next year | To celebrate the winner | To count the votes twice | *To cancel, as if it never counted
exercise: Henry VIII wanted the Pope to annul his marriage. What did he want? | For the Pope to get married | For the marriage to last forever | *For the marriage to be declared never valid | For the Pope to visit England
exercise: «The annulment of the contract was announced today.» Which word is the noun? | today | *annulment | announced | contract
test: «The shop had to annul the sale because the price on the sign was wrong.» Why did the shop annul the sale? | To make the sale last longer | To move the sale to next week | *Because the sale was declared never to have counted, due to the wrong price | To give everyone a free gift
test: Which word is closest in meaning to annul? | Repeat | *Cancel | Decorate | Celebrate
exam: «The court may annul a contract if one side was tricked.» What does the court do when it annuls a contract? | Reads the contract aloud to everyone | Makes the contract longer | *Declares that the contract never counted | Signs it again with new names
